  "name": "Example: Solving an Inequality Involving an Even Power Compared To a Negative Number",
  "problem": "Solve $(5x-1)^6 + 5 \\geq -4.$",
  "worked_solution": "Isolating the sixth-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5x-1)^{6}+5 & \\ge -4 \\\\ (5x-1)^{6} & \\ge -9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $(5x - 1)^{6} \\geq 0$ for all values of $x$ because the power $(6)$ is even.\n\nTherefore, the solution to the given inequality is all real numbers.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
